**Securities Investment Due Diligence and Examination Records Policy**

**Section 1: Purpose and Scope**

This policy establishes the requirements for conducting due diligence and maintaining examination records for securities investments made by [National Bank Name] in accordance with 12 CFR 9.18 and 12 CFR 9.19.

**Section 2: Definitions**

For purposes of this policy, the following definitions apply:

* "Due diligence" means the process of investigating and evaluating the risks and opportunities of a securities investment to ensure that the investment is appropriate for [National Bank Name] and consistent with applicable laws and regulations.
* "Examination records" means the records maintained by [National Bank Name] that document the due diligence process and the results of the examination of a securities investment.

**Section 3: Due Diligence Requirements**

(a) Due diligence for all securities investments shall be conducted in accordance with the requirements of 12 CFR 9.18 and 12 CFR 9.19.
(b) Due diligence for all securities investments shall be conducted by or under the direction of the board of directors or a committee thereof.
(c) Due diligence for all securities investments shall be documented in the examination records.

**Section 4: Examination Records**

(a) Examination records shall be maintained for all securities investments and shall include:
(1) The name and title of the person or persons conducting the due diligence;
(2) The date(s) of the due diligence;
(3) A description of the securities investment;
(4) The investment decision, including the amount of the investment and the price at which it was made;
(5) The investment strategy for the securities investment;
(6) An analysis of the risks and opportunities of the securities investment;
(7) The expected return on the securities investment;
(8) The expected term of the securities investment;
(9) The estimated market risk, credit risk, price volatility, liquidity risk, and other relevant risks of the securities investment;
(10) The estimated return of principal and return of capital of the securities investment;
(11) The estimated costs of the securities investment, including fees and expenses;
(12) The estimated tax consequences of the securities investment;
