3. **Notification of Failure to Receive Funds or Securities**: A broker or dealer shall promptly notify a customer of the failure of the customer to make full payment for securities purchased or to deliver full payment for securities sold, or shall otherwise provide the customer with the information required by this section, on the same business day that the broker or dealer notifies the clearing corporation of the failure, or if not possible, no later than the end of the next business day after the broker or dealer notifies the clearing corporation of the failure. (17 CFR 240.17Adj-1(c))

